gosh seam 05: The core's build is told where gosh's parts are.

For:   REQ6/SHAPE-5. gosh's code is in a directory per part, named for the part, outside the
       core. tools/build.sh copies those directories into its copy of the core's src/, and this
       patch has the core's build go into them.
What:  src/forwarding is added to the directories built (after network, which it uses, and before
       the programs), and its Makefile to the files configure writes. One line of each kind is
       added for each part as it arrives.
Where: configure.ac (AC_CONFIG_FILES); src/Makefile.am (SUBDIRS).
Kind:  additions only. Written for gosh: the fork instead put every added file into the core's
       own networking library, which is how a file copier came to live there.
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -588,6 +588,7 @@
   src/fuzz/Makefile
   src/include/Makefile
   src/network/Makefile
+  src/forwarding/Makefile
   src/protobufs/Makefile
   src/statesync/Makefile
   src/terminal/Makefile
--- a/src/Makefile.am
+++ b/src/Makefile.am
@@ -1 +1 @@
-SUBDIRS = include protobufs util crypto terminal network statesync frontend examples tests fuzz
+SUBDIRS = include protobufs util crypto terminal network forwarding statesync frontend examples tests fuzz
